WEBVTT

00:03.920 --> 00:05.320
Now I'm going to show you how it looks like.

00:05.360 --> 00:06.560
Usually in companies.

00:06.560 --> 00:08.520
So we have our data inside the database.

00:08.520 --> 00:14.240
And then you will have multiple people with multiple roles that are just writing different sqls in order

00:14.240 --> 00:15.240
to talk to the data.

00:15.240 --> 00:21.160
But now not only employees and people interact with the database, you could build a website or an application

00:21.160 --> 00:24.960
that as well interacts with the database by sending different sqls.

00:24.960 --> 00:29.160
And of course depends on how many people are interacting with the application and the websites.

00:29.160 --> 00:33.880
It might generate really massive amounts of sqls that sends to the database.

00:33.880 --> 00:39.040
And not only that, you might have as well tools in order to do data visualizations where you have like

00:39.080 --> 00:45.600
a dashboard or a report, maybe created using power BI or Tableau, and it is used by stakeholders and

00:45.600 --> 00:47.400
managers in order to make decisions.

00:47.400 --> 00:52.840
And as well, those tools will be connected to the database and creating Sqls.

00:52.840 --> 00:57.800
So now as you can see, we have a lot of interactions with the database from people, applications,

00:57.800 --> 00:58.440
tools.

00:58.560 --> 01:02.840
A lot of things are generating sqls and interacting with the database.

01:02.840 --> 01:06.000
But the database is just a container and storage, right.

01:06.000 --> 01:09.830
So we need something software that manage all those requests.

01:09.830 --> 01:14.190
And that's why we have something called Database Management System DBMs.

01:14.350 --> 01:18.830
So it is a software that can manage all those different requests to our database.

01:18.830 --> 01:22.670
And it's going to make the priority which SQL must be executed first.

01:22.710 --> 01:28.230
This software can as well manage the security whether the SQL is allowed to be executed in the first

01:28.230 --> 01:28.670
place.

01:28.750 --> 01:34.750
So my friends, the DBMs is the software that can manage the database and now we are not done yet.

01:34.750 --> 01:35.790
There is something missing.

01:35.790 --> 01:36.670
So we have our data.

01:36.670 --> 01:37.630
We have the software.

01:37.630 --> 01:39.630
What is missing here is the hardware.

01:39.630 --> 01:45.990
So in real companies we cannot run that on our PC because first our PC is weak and as well it goes offline.

01:45.990 --> 01:48.230
That's why we need a server server.

01:48.230 --> 01:52.470
It is like a very powerful PC and as well it lives 24 over seven.

01:52.510 --> 01:53.910
So it is always available.

01:53.910 --> 01:58.830
And here we can decide whether we can have a server inside the company, or we can use cloud services

01:58.830 --> 02:00.990
in order to run our database.

02:00.990 --> 02:05.590
So my friends, so far what we have learned the database, it is a container to store the data, the

02:05.590 --> 02:10.950
SQL, it is the language in order to talk to the database, the DBMs, it is the manager.

02:10.950 --> 02:13.390
It manages the database and the server.

02:13.390 --> 02:16.430
It is the physical machine where the database lives.

02:16.430 --> 02:17.910
So this is how it looks like.
